gofer_add_todo	Add a todo to a plan. Omit job_id for a plain checklist item, or set it to bind the todo to a job run. The dispatch fields (assignee/project/template/vars/verify/review/runner/cwd/timeout_sec/model/budget) describe how the item runs once it turns ready; the item is created pending.
gofer_answer_interaction	Answer a pending interaction on a running job so the agent can continue.
gofer_ask_human	Block and ask a HUMAN a question when a plan hits a decision point; the call returns when a person answers on the web console (bell / plan page) or the timeout expires. Returns {state:"answered", answer, answered_by} or {state:"expired"} — on expired, continue with your prepared fallback (e.g. recommended option, or mark the todo skipped+note); never block forever. Set timeout_sec within your host's own tool-call timeout.
gofer_attach_job	Attach an existing job to a plan by id. Returns the plan header.
gofer_cancel_job	Request cancellation of a running job and return its current state.
gofer_comment	Comment on a job, plan or todo (scope=job|plan|todo, id, body) in its thread. You speak as the agent of the job this process runs in (GOFER_JOB_ID; pass as_job to name it explicitly) — the comment is RECORDED and dispatches nothing: only a human's @mention starts a job. Use it to report progress, answer a human in the thread, or leave the reasoning behind a decision.
gofer_create_plan	Create a lightweight plan grouping header and return it. Use plan_id from the result to attach jobs or submit jobs with plan_id set. Without supervisor_session_id the plan is bound to the calling agent's own terminal session when gofer knows it (supervisor_note says so); pass no_supervisor=true to skip.
gofer_dispatch_todo	Dispatch a todo's assigned agent NOW, regardless of the item's status (the explicit fallback to "ready + assigned"): starts a job for it and returns {todo, job, dispatched, reason}. Needs an assignee and no live job — when nothing is started, reason says why.
gofer_get_artifacts	List a finished job's captured artifact files (name/size/mtime under its result dir).
gofer_get_interactions	List a job's running-time interactions (pending questions and their answers).
gofer_get_job	Get the current state of a job by id.
gofer_get_plan	Get a plan with its jobs and a live status roll-up {total,queued,running,done,failed}.
gofer_get_result	Get a finished job's structured result.json content, as a raw JSON string.
gofer_issue_brief	Handoff brief (接手包) of a repository issue — the same text as `gofer issue brief <id>`: the issue, its parent/siblings/deps, design docs that name it, related commits and code entries, linked jobs / plans, applicable memories and takeover hints. Read this first when taking over an issue. Uses the repository tracker of this process's cwd.
gofer_issue_get	Read one tracker issue in full from the server's mirror (read-only). Give tracker_id when the same id exists in several repos.
gofer_issue_list	List tracker issues from the server's mirror (read-only). Filters: project, tracker_id / repo (rel path), status (open|in_progress|closed…), type, tags[] (all must match), query (id / title / description substring), limit (default 50, max 200). Returns brief rows plus total / truncated.
gofer_job_end	End a resident ACP session job and release its lock.
gofer_job_follow_up	Queue, list, or drop follow-up requests for a running job; queued requests continue its session when it ends.
gofer_job_say	Send another message to the same resident ACP session job.
gofer_job_set	Set or clear a job title. A job credential may only change its own job.
gofer_list_agents	List the configured/built-in agents with their availability probe.
gofer_list_comments	Read the comment thread of a job, plan or todo (scope=job|plan|todo, id), oldest first — including the jobs a human's @mentions dispatched.
gofer_list_pending_interactions	List pending interactions across active jobs (for a supervisor agent to discover questions awaiting an answer).
gofer_list_plans	List plans, optionally requiring every tag and matching a title or id keyword.
gofer_list_projects	List the registered projects and their agent/runner allowlists.
gofer_list_templates	List the task-book templates a project can be driven with (name/source/path/desc/vars). Submit one with gofer_run_job template=<name> vars={...}.
gofer_memory_candidate_adopt	Adopt (accept) a knowledge candidate on a person's behalf: write its text as a server memory under key (kind rule|note, default note; summary required for content > 200 chars) in the job's project scope (or global=true / project=<key>). An existing key is refused. Job credentials are refused.
gofer_memory_candidate_reject	Reject a knowledge candidate (nothing is written). Job credentials are refused.
gofer_memory_candidates	List knowledge candidates: the 「## 可复用经验」 report items of delivered jobs, waiting for a person to accept (it becomes a server memory, source job:<id>) or reject. Filters: job_id, project, status (pending default | accepted | rejected | all).
gofer_memory_flag	Report an injected memory / rule as out of date instead of silently working around it: it is marked 「⚠ 待复核（reason）」 wherever it is injected until a human reviews it. Omit scope for the repository tracker of this process's cwd; scope=global|project (+scope_key) for server memories. reason is required.
gofer_memory_get	Read one server global or project memory.
gofer_memory_list	List server global or project memories, optionally filtered by keyword and tags.
gofer_memory_rm	Soft-delete a server global or project memory.
gofer_memory_set	Write a server global or project memory. Optional title (<= 80 chars, one line) is the display name; the key stays the identifier.
gofer_plan_brief	Handoff brief (接手包) of a plan — the same text as `gofer plan brief <id>`: fields, todos (status / deps / acceptance / job outcome), handoff note and a short brief of each issue it names.
gofer_plan_handoff	Read or write a plan's versioned Markdown handoff note. action=get reads the latest or version; action=set appends a version using expected_version.
gofer_plan_run	Start a plan's dependency chain: queue every pending item whose `after` dependencies are done or skipped and that has an assignee (root items included), release a pause/block, and return the plan header {plan_id, status, paused, blocked_todo, ...}. Items then run one after another as each finishes; a failed chain item parks the plan (status=blocked, blocked_todo names it).
gofer_punt_interaction	As a supervisor, mark a pending interaction as needing a human (高危/拿不准, 留给人处理): leaves it pending for a person and stops the supervisor being re-woken for it. Use this instead of guessing when you can't safely answer.
gofer_refs	List visible jobs, plans, todos and comments that reference an issue, job, plan, todo or workflow id.
gofer_reject_job	Reject a job awaiting human review (needs_review): record why it is unacceptable, and with resume=true start a continuation that uses the note as its prompt. Not for a job awaiting approval (hold): approving or rejecting that is a person's decision — withdraw your own held job with gofer_cancel_job.
gofer_run_job	Submit an agent/exec job in a project and return its initial state (status, id). Set plan_id to group it under a plan. Set budget {max_tokens (input+output+cache), max_cost_usd, max_turns (model requests)} to cap its spend: the job is killed and fails with failure_class=budget when a limit is crossed (0/omitted = unlimited; the agent must report readable usage). Inside budget, agent_tokens / agent_cost_usd are a SOFT budget the agent enforces on itself (it winds the run up and reports; set them below the hard max_*): only agents with an agent_budget mapping (e.g. suga) take them, any other agent is refused. Set from_session=<session id> to open a NEW agent session that inherits an earlier session's context (cli-agent with from_session_args only; not combinable with a resume). Timeout_sec above the applicable limit is clamped, reported in the result (timeout_sec, requested_timeout_sec, timeout_clamped, timeout_limit_source project|server, timeout_limit_key); set strict_timeout=true to refuse instead. Set hold=true (with hold_reason, optional hold_timeout_sec) for an outward or irreversible step (e.g. git push) your own permissions stop: the job parks in awaiting_approval and runs only after a PERSON approves it in the web console — never approve it yourself; withdraw it with gofer_cancel_job.
gofer_session_ask	带话: deliver a short message to a RUNNING session over the existing relay channels ("the resource arrived, you can continue"). id is a terminal session id or an ACP / pty session job id. A session that is not online is an error (nothing is queued — tell the person instead). The message is logged on the session's work item as yours. Not for asking a session to report — use gofer_work_request_report for that.
gofer_session_find	Find which live session works on something (read-only): query matches topics / session names / projects, path matches the sessions' scopes. Returns ranked sessions with the reasons they matched; maybe_offline marks one that stopped heart-beating. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_get	Read one terminal agent session (read-only; id may be a unique prefix).
gofer_session_list	List registered terminal agent sessions (read-only): id, agent, project, runner, cwd, title, state, last message, last seen.
gofer_session_mail_ack	Acknowledge a letter as its recipient without sending a reply. done=false means received; done=true means processed.
gofer_session_mail_cancel	Withdraw a letter that has not been delivered yet (an already delivered letter cannot be cancelled). Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_mail_list	List letters you sent or received (read-only). box: in | out | all (default), plus optional thread / state / session filters and limit. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_mail_pause	Pause mailbox delivery to one session; letters stay queued until resumed. Only its owner (or a caller with session.reply.others) may change it.
gofer_session_mail_read	Read one letter in full. Reading marks it read as its recipient, so it is not injected into a later turn again. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_mail_reply	Answer a letter in its thread; the answer goes back to the sender's address. This is the only way to answer a letter. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_mail_resume	Resume mailbox delivery to one session, preserving queued letter order.
gofer_session_mail_send	Send a letter to another session, a session job, a gofer mail agent or yourself. to: session:<sid> | job:<id> | agent:<name>[@<project>] | topic:<keyword> | path:<sub-path> | caller (your own capture box); give several, or an each:topic:<kw> / each:path:<sub> / each:project:<key> / each:agent:<name> selector, to send one letter to every match. Only a unique recipient is delivered to; an ambiguous topic / path address is held in the capture box; an ambiguous or unknown session prefix is an error with its candidates (held=true in the answer — pick one and send again with session:<sid>). A letter arrives in the recipient's next turn wrapped in a <gofer-mail> tag; it is not a user message. urgent=true asks for delivery inside the running turn. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_screen	Read the tail of what another session shows right now (read-only): its recent relay turns (agent question / human answer, the same rows gofer_session_get returns) or, for a session taken over by an interactive pty job, that job's terminal transcript. Text has ANSI escapes removed; n bounds the lines (default 50). Never writes to the session.
gofer_session_set_topic	Record what THIS session works on so others (and the person) can find it: topic is one short sentence, scope are the project-relative sub-paths you own (clear_scope empties them). Omitted fields stay unchanged. The current session comes from the environment (session_id overrides); an ended session is refused. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_session_wait	Block until another session reaches a state (read-only): until is idle (it is free — default), waiting_reply (it asks the human something) or ended (it is gone); a comma-separated list waits for any of them. Returns the session and reached=false when timeout_sec ran out — a timeout is an outcome, not an error. Already being in that state returns at once. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_set_plan_notify	Turn a plan's end-notification switch on or off (on|off): with it on, every job the plan dispatches tells the plan's supervisor session that it ended, through the session messenger.
gofer_set_plan_supervisor_session	Bind or clear the authenticated terminal session that supervises plan dispatches. Requires an authenticated HTTP-backed Gofer server.
gofer_tail_log	Return the tail of a job's stdout/stderr log (capped at 256KB by default).
gofer_update_plan_tags	Replace or remove a plan's tags and return the updated plan.
gofer_update_todo	Update a todo by todo_id: move it along its lifecycle (status: pending|ready|doing|done|skipped — doing stamps started_at, done/skipped stamp done_at) and/or set a short outcome note, and/or set the dispatch fields (assignee/project/template/vars/verify/review/runner/cwd/timeout_sec/model/budget). A write that makes the item ready AND assigned dispatches it immediately (a job starts; the item turns doing). Returns the updated todo.
gofer_wakeup_create	Register a wakeup on a job: an event subscription or timer that RESUMES that job when it fires. kind=at (at, unix seconds), every (every_sec >= 60), cron (cron + optional timezone) or event (event_types from job.terminal|job.verify_finished|job.needs_review|job.reviewed|job.fell_back|job.stalled|interaction.answered|session.takeover_released; optional filter_job_id + filter_status). instruction is the prompt the continuation receives; mode once (default) or continuous. From inside a job, pass that job's own id to be woken after it ends.
gofer_wakeup_disable	Disable a wakeup by id so it stops firing (it stays listed; enabling again re-arms a timer from now).
gofer_wakeup_list	List a job's wakeups with their state (enabled, next_run_at, fired_count, coalesced_count, continuation_job_id).
gofer_work_capture	Jot an idea / issue / request / note into the human's capture box (a quick record, not a work item you are doing). text is required; kind is idea|issue|request|note (default note); project is optional. The entry waits for the human to sort it; nothing runs. Returns the new entry (its id and status).
gofer_work_get	Read one work item with its journal (newest entries, oldest first), all sessions (current and past) and links.
gofer_work_list	List the human's work items (what they are doing, across terminal sessions) with the header counts. Filters: status[] (active|needs_me|waiting_resource|needs_onsite|review|parked|done|dropped), project, workspace, unsorted, query, due (reminder/park deadline passed), include_closed. Each item carries goal / blocker / next step, its current sessions and links.
gofer_work_note	Append a note to a work item's journal (append-only). level is optional: milestone (a real progress point, shown on the Today lane and the default timeline) or detail (default).
gofer_work_report	Report where a work item stands (goal / status / blocker / next / summary; session_id names the reporting session; request is the request id from a report / hand-over request you were asked to answer — it marks that request answered). Use it when asked to report. status active means 'the blocker is gone' and releases a status the human set; any other status is ignored while the human's own status stands, and done/dropped are never taken from a report.
gofer_work_request_report	Ask a work item's running session(s) to report (kind report, default) or to write a hand-over (kind handoff) through the request ledger; the session answers with gofer_work_report / `gofer work report --request <id>`. A session that is not running is tidied up instead. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_work_requests	Read the work request ledger (read-only): the report / hand-over / tidy-up asks and what became of them (pending|sent|answered|failed|expired). id limits it to one work item, active only the in-flight ones.
gofer_work_summarize	Tidy a work item up now: a cheap one-shot read-only model reads the session transcript tail and fills goal / blocker / next. Fields a person or the session wrote become suggestions for the person to adopt (never overwritten); the status is only a hint. Returns the ledger request that tracks it. Needs a running gofer server.
gofer_work_update	Change a work item's descriptive fields (title, goal, blocker_kind/blocker_text, next_step, summary, project_key, workspace, priority, park_until / remind_at as unix seconds, park_note, unsorted). Pass rev to get an optimistic-lock check (conflict if the item changed). It does NOT set the status: a status is the human's call or goes through gofer_work_report, which respects the status a person set.
